{
  "README": [
    "Screens the dev mock replays so every agent cornus can classify has something to look at.",
    "",
    "One entry is one moment of one agent's terminal: the OSC window title it sets, the lines it",
    "paints, and the state the bundled manifest classifies that into. The mock plays an agent's",
    "entries in order (working, then blocked awaiting an answer, then idle) and REPORTS THE STATE",
    "FROM THE ENTRY rather than inventing one — see startAgentDemo in faketerm.ts.",
    "",
    "That is only honest if the entries are true, so they are checked from the Go side, twice:",
    "  pkg/agentdetect/screens_test.go            the declared rule is the one that fires",
    "  cmd/cornus/internal/webbff/agentscreens_test.go   the same bytes through a real session",
    "The second is the one that makes 'end to end' mean anything: it renders the screen on the",
    "same headless VT100 the BFF uses, sniffs the title off the same OSC scanner, and reads the",
    "state off the session list — so an entry that only classifies as a bare string does not pass.",
    "",
    "Authoring rules, each learned from a failure:",
    "  - No trailing whitespace on a screen line. The renderer right-trims every row, so a line",
    "    with one would reach the two checks differently.",
    "  - At most 12 lines. detBottomLines keeps only the last 12 rows; lines above that are",
    "    invisible to the detector and would make an entry pass for a reason the mock cannot show.",
    "  - Keep lines under 80 columns, the detector's default screen width. A wrapped line is a",
    "    different line, and a rule anchored with ^ or $ stops matching it.",
    "  - `rule` names the rule that must WIN, not merely one that matches. Several rules can fire",
    "    on one screen; asserting the winner is what catches a screen that lands on the right",
    "    state through the wrong evidence.",
    "  - An agent whose manifest reads its state off the OSC title (amp, claude, codex, grok,",
    "    hermes) needs a title that agrees with the state on EVERY entry. The detector never",
    "    clears a title it has seen, so a stale working title outranks the next screen."
  ],
